                                  "line_count":  160,
                                  "evidence_status":  "observed",
                                  "content_truncated":  false,
                                  "content":  "# PROMETHEUS V2 — MEDIA PRODUCTION CONTRACT V1\n\n## Objective\n\nDefine the canonical audiovisual production model used by Prometheus V2.\n\nThe system does not treat a video as a single opaque file.\n\nA production is a graph of:\n\nRESEARCH\n→ SCRIPT\n→ SCENE_PLAN\n→ VOICE\n→ VISUALS\n→ MUSIC\n→ SFX\n→ CAPTIONS\n→ EDITING_BLUEPRINT\n→ RENDER\n→ AUDIO MASTER\n→ QA\n→ VIDEO_MASTER\n\nEvery material output is an artifact.\n\nEvery artifact is traceable to:\n\n- run_id\n- stage\n- artifact_id\n- object_key\n- SHA-256\n- contract version\n- provider where applicable\n\n## Core principle\n\nThe Editing Blueprint is the canonical source of temporal truth.\n\nThe renderer does not invent editorial decisions.\n\nIt receives:\n\n1. assets\n2. timing\n3. transitions\n4. captions\n5. sound design\n6. audio mix parameters\n7. delivery profile\n\nand renders exactly what the blueprint specifies.\n\n## Audio\n\nThe final master is measured using EBU R128-compatible analysis.\n\nPrometheus V2 uses a configurable loudness target, with the initial production profile targeting:\n\n- Integrated loudness: -14 LUFS\n- Maximum true peak: -1 dBTP\n- LRA target: 11 LU\n\nThese are engineering defaults, not claims about platform algorithms.\n\nVoice receives priority over music and SFX.\n\nMusic ducking and SFX levels are explicit blueprint parameters.\n\n## Video\n\nCanonical short-form delivery profile:\n\n- 1080 × 1920\n- vertical\n- H.264\n- AAC\n- 48 kHz\n- MP4\n- default 30 fps\n\nThe profile is versioned and may evolve without changing the underlying contracts.\n\n## Captions\n\nCaptions are not generated by the renderer.\n\nThe Caption Plan defines:\n\n- text\n- timing\n- emphasis\n- position\n- animation\n\nThe renderer only executes the plan.\n\n## QA\n\nA VIDEO_MASTER cannot be considered production-ready unless:\n\n- video stream exists\n- audio stream exists\n- container is valid\n- duration is valid\n- A/V duration difference is within tolerance\n- required artifacts exist\n- SHA-256 is available\n- caption constraints pass\n- audio master measurements pass\n- artifact registry is coherent\n\n## Determinism\n\nWhere possible, rendering must be deterministic.\n\nThe same:\n\n- Editing Blueprint\n- asset versions\n- renderer version\n- profile version\n\nmust produce reproducible output metadata.\n\nThe exact binary hash may differ if the encoder/runtime changes, therefore renderer version is part of the evidence.\n\n## Separation of responsibilities\n\nn8n:\n- orchestration\n- state transitions\n- retries\n- dependency management\n- provider routing\n- calling execution services\n\nFFmpeg:\n- media rendering\n- compositing\n- encoding\n- audio processing\n- loudness processing\n\nPostgreSQL:\n- control plane\n- state\n- contracts\n- evidence\n- registry\n\nStorage Adapter:\n- physical object storage\n\nSeaweedFS:\n- physical S3-compatible storage\n\nNo AI-Lab component may directly mutate Prometheus production state.\r\n",
